Subject: [PATCH] supply native standard memory declarations to original KPAD

Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Whole Matching KPAD source remains authoritative for filtering, sampling,
repeat, acceleration and IR decisions. Modern C99 compilers require the actual
memcpy/memset declarations. Add only the native standard header; console source
and every original method body remain unchanged. WPAD hardware is supplied below
this SDK code by a separate bounded native provider.

Refreshed for decomp 9046e67a: upstream declares sqrt through MSL's
internal/fdlibm.h, which native builds do not have on their path; the native
branch takes it from the host <math.h>, as the former local declaration did.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/kpad/KPAD.c b/src/RVL_SDK/kpad/KPAD.c
index ac2e40f..0ace788 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/kpad/KPAD.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/kpad/KPAD.c
@@ -1,6 +1,15 @@
 #include <revolution/kpad.h>
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+#include <string.h>
+#endif
+
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// The host C library supplies sqrt, as the earlier local declaration did.
+#include <math.h>
+#else
 #include <internal/fdlibm.h>
+#endif
 
 #if defined(VERSION_R4QE01) || defined(VERSION_R4QJ01)
 static const char* __KPADVersion = "<< RVL_SDK - KPAD \trelease build: May 17 2007 15:52:00 (0x4199_60831) >>";
